# Git attributes for radstorm
#
# Purpose:
#   Ensures shell scripts and FreeRADIUS config files always use LF line endings
#   in the repository and when checked out, regardless of the developer's OS.
#   CRLF endings in FreeRADIUS users/config files cause parsing failures.
#
# Related: test/docker/freeradius/users, test/docker/seed/generate-users.sh
# Briefing: .orchestration/briefings/1e-docker-rig.md
# Contract: Shell scripts and RADIUS config always LF; source files auto-detected.

# Default: auto-detect text files and normalise to LF in repo
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts: always LF
*.sh text eol=lf

# FreeRADIUS config and data files: always LF (CRLF breaks parsing)
test/docker/freeradius/users text eol=lf
test/docker/freeradius/*.conf text eol=lf
test/docker/freeradius/sites-enabled/* text eol=lf

# TOML, YAML, Dockerfile: LF
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# CSV fixtures: LF
*.csv text eol=lf

# Go source: LF
*.go text eol=lf

# TypeScript / JavaScript: LF
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Markdown: LF
*.md text eol=lf

# Binaries: keep binary
*.exe binary
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
